# Extra specifications that are not part of the generated W3C + Specref dump.
#
# RDF Messages is a Community Group living document, so it has no W3C TR
# shortlink. The RDF Stream Processing CG itself already comes from the W3C API
# crawl; this file adds the document and the ex:specification link that puts it
# on both the group page and the specification list.
#
# Source: https://w3c-cg.github.io/rsp/spec/messages
#
# Data spaces batch — from the Gaia-X TechX26 talk "An ODRL Profile to join
# them all for Data Spaces" by Joaquín Salvachúa and Andrés Muñoz (UPM).
#
# Source: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ysykboeFPs8
# Slides: https://gaia-x.eu/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/2.4-An-ODRL-Profile-to-join-them-all-for-Data-Spaces.pdf
#
# The talk links https://w3c.github.io/odrl/profile-bigdata/; that document now
# says it is superseded by https://w3c.github.io/odrl/profile-dataspaces/. Both
# stay in the catalog because the linked URL is still live. ODRL 2.2 is the
# Recommendation the profiles extend; it is not in the W3C API dump, so it is
# added here.
#
# Seeded with `devbox run seed` (see devbox.json).

